/// sentinel for the properties it resets. The table holds whether Chrome accepted the declaration, and the values Chrome reported that this library reports
/// too (compared after trimming, lower-casing and writing numbers canonically). Not listed: values that Chrome serializes differently from the specified text
/// (<c>steps(4, jump-end)</c> is <c>steps(4)</c>, <c>linear(0, 1)</c> is <c>linear(0 0%, 1 100%)</c>, <c>100ms</c> is <c>0.1s</c>, <c>calc()</c> is folded) and
/// <c>animation-duration</c>, which Chrome reports as <c>0s</c> where the specification's computed value is <c>auto</c>.
